{"document_id": "f057ebca-308d-48c8-8e96-e7fbdda1368e", "crop": "mango", "organization": "TNAU", "source": "TNAU", "source_url": "https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/mango_7.html", "title": "TNAU Agritech Portal :: Crop Protection", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-06T23:40:47.782952", "content": "| ![TNAU Agritech Portal](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/index/cp_index.jpg)  |  \n| --- |  \n|  [Home](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/index.html \"Home\") | [About Us](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/about_us/abt_us.html \"About Us\") | [Success Stories](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/success_stories/success_index.html \"Success Stories\") | [Farmers Association](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_association/farm_assoct.html \"Farmer's Association\") | [Farmers' Innovation](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_innovations/farm_innovations.html) | [Publications](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/tnau_publish.html \"TNAU Publications\") | [Contact](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/contact.html \"Contact Us\")  |   |  \n|    \nHorticultural crops :: Fruits:: Mango   \n  \n |   \n |  **Sooty mould:**_Capnodium mangiferae_  |  \n| --- |  \n|  **Symptoms**\n  * The fungi produce mycelium which is superficial and dark. They row on sugary secretions of the plant hoppers. Black encrustation is formed which affect the photosynthetic activity.\n  * The fungus grows on the leaf surface on the sugary substances secreted by jassids, aphids and scale insects.\n\n  \n | ![](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/mango/sootymould/crop_prot_crop%20diseases_fruits_mango_clip_image032_0000.jpg)  | ![](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/mango/sootymould/crop_prot_crop%20diseases_fruits_mango_clip_image030_0000.jpg)  | ![](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/mango/sootymould/ooty_%20mould_%20on_%20ripe_fruit.jpg)  | ![](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/mango/sootymould/ooty_mould_on_mature_fruit.jpg)  |  \n| --- | --- | --- | --- |  \n| **Healthy leaf**  | **Infected leaf**  | **Sooty mould on mature fruit**  |  \n |  \n|  **Management**\n  * Management should be done for insects and sooty moulds simultaneously. \n  * Controlling of insect by spraying systemic insecticides like methyl dematon\n  * After that spray starch solution (1kg Starch/Maida in 5 litres of water. Boiled and dilute to 20 liters)\n  * Starch dries and forms flake which are removed along with the fungus.\n\n |  \n |  \n |  \n |  \n| \n* * *\n[Home](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/index.html \"Home\") | [About Us](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/about_us/abt_us.html \"About Us\") | [Success Stories](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/success_stories/success_index.html \"Success Stories\") | [Farmers Association](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_association/farm_assoct.html \"Farmers Association\") | [Farmers' Innovation](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_innovations/farm_innovations.html) | [Publications](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/tnau_publish.html \"TNAU Publications\") | [Contact Us ](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/contact.html \"Contact Us\") © 2015 TNAU. All Rights Reserved.  |\n", "html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd\"><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head>\n<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"Agriculture, TNAU, Precision Farming, Organic Farming,Daily News Paper Farm Information, Daily Market Information, TNAU Weather,Horticulture, Organic Agriculture, Agriculture Engineering, Agriculture Marketing, Seed Certification, Crop Protection, Crop Insurance,Fishery, Forestry, Animal Husbandry, Sericulture, Commmunity Radio,KVK, E Extension Center,Govt Schemes &amp; Services,Variety Releases\">\n<title>TNAU Agritech Portal :: Crop Protection</title>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">\n<!--\nfunction MM_openBrWindow(theURL,winName,features) { //v2.0\n  window.open(theURL,winN